---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Journal — Insights on Architectural Model Making | Carve Model"
  description="Practical guidance on physical models, project planning, materials, fabrication, and digital-to-physical production—along with news, events, and observations from Carve Model."
  canonicalPath="/blog"
  ogTitle="Journal | Carve Model"
  ogDescription="Practical guidance on physical models, project planning, materials, fabrication, and digital-to-physical production."
  active="blog"
  imageSlot={true}
>
<Fragment slot="head">
<link rel="alternate" type="application/rss+xml" title="Carve Model Blog" href="/rss.xml">
<style>
.page-hero{padding-top:clamp(3rem,6vw,5rem);padding-bottom:clamp(2.5rem,4vw,3rem);border-bottom:1px solid var(--cm-line-faint);}
.page-hero h1{margin-top:1.4rem;}.page-hero p{margin-top:1.4rem;}
.feat{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 0.9fr;gap:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.5rem);align-items:center;padding-top:1.6rem;padding-bottom:clamp(1.3rem,2vw,1.8rem);margin-top:1.6rem;}
.feat image-slot{width:100%;aspect-ratio:16/10;}
.feat-visual{position:relative;}
.feat-visual .feat-photo{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:16/10;object-fit:cover;object-position:50% center;border-radius:var(--r-sm);}
.feat-visual .corner{position:absolute;width:14px;height:14px;border:1px solid var(--cm-silver);opacity:0.5;z-index:3;}
.feat-visual .corner.tl{top:-1px;left:-1px;border-right:0;border-bottom:0;}
.feat-visual .corner.br{bottom:-1px;right:-1px;border-left:0;border-top:0;}
.feat h2{font-size:clamp(1.6rem,2.8vw,2.4rem);letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin-top:1rem;}
.feat p{margin-top:1rem;color:var(--cm-gray-300);}
.feat .meta{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.72rem;color:var(--cm-text-subtle);letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;}
.feat a.read{display:inline-flex;gap:0.4rem;margin-top:1.1rem;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.75rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.06em;color:var(--cm-silver);}
.latest-post{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 0.9fr;gap:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.5rem);align-items:center;margin-top:1.6rem;}
@media(max-width:820px){.latest-post{grid-template-columns:1fr;}}
.latest-post .latest-photo{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;aspect-ratio:16/10;object-fit:cover;object-position:50% center;border-radius:var(--r-sm);}
.latest-post .meta{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.72rem;color:var(--cm-text-subtle);letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;}
.latest-post h3{font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:clamp(1.6rem,2.8vw,2.4rem);font-weight:var(--w-bold);margin-top:0.9rem;letter-spacing:-0.02em;line-height:1.08;}
.latest-post p{margin-top:0.9rem;color:var(--cm-gray-300);}
.latest-post a.read{display:inline-flex;gap:0.4rem;margin-top:1.1rem;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.75rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.06em;color:var(--cm-silver);}
.feat-visual .mock{width:100%;background:var(--cm-ink-850);border:1px solid var(--cm-border-strong);border-radius:var(--r-md);overflow:hidden;box-shadow:var(--shadow-lg);font-size:0.78rem;}
.feat-visual .mock__bar{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.5rem;padding:0.7rem 0.9rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--cm-border);background:var(--cm-ink-800);}
.feat-visual .mock__bar i{width:9px;height:9px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--cm-ink-500);display:block;}
.feat-visual .mock__bar span{margin-left:auto;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.66rem;color:var(--cm-text-subtle);}
.feat-visual .mock__body{padding:1rem;display:grid;grid-template-columns:0.8fr 1.2fr;gap:0.8rem;}
.feat-visual .mock__side{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.5rem;}
.feat-visual .mock__row{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.55rem;padding:0.5rem 0.6rem;border-radius:var(--r-sm);color:var(--cm-gray-300);font-size:0.74rem;}
.feat-visual .mock__row.active{background:var(--cm-surface-2);color:var(--cm-text-strong);}
.feat-visual .mock__row b{width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--cm-silver);display:block;}
.feat-visual .mock__main{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.6rem;}
.feat-visual .mock__card{background:var(--cm-ink-800);border:1px solid var(--cm-border);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:0.75rem;}
.feat-visual .mock__progress{height:5px;background:var(--cm-ink-600);border-radius:99px;margin-top:0.5rem;overflow:hidden;}
.feat-visual .mock__progress i{display:block;height:100%;background:var(--cm-silver);}
.feat-visual .mock__k{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.64rem;color:var(--cm-text-subtle);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.06em;}
.feat-visual .mock__v{color:var(--cm-text-strong);font-weight:var(--w-semibold);margin-top:2px;}
.posts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:2rem;margin-top:1.6rem;align-items:stretch;}
.post{border-top:1px solid var(--cm-border);padding-top:1.4rem;display:flex;flex-direction:column;}
.post .meta{font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.7rem;color:var(--cm-text-subtle);letter-spacing:0.04em;text-transform:uppercase;}
.post h3{font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:1.25rem;font-weight:var(--w-semibold);margin-top:0.9rem;letter-spacing:-0.01em;line-height:1.2;min-height:3rem;}
.post p{margin-top:0.7rem;color:var(--cm-text-muted);font-size:0.92rem;}
.post a.read{display:inline-flex;gap:0.4rem;margin-top:auto;padding-top:1rem;font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.72rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.06em;color:var(--cm-silver);}
.hero__cta{display:flex;gap:0.9rem;flex-wrap:nowrap;margin-top:1.8rem;}
@media(max-width:560px){.hero__cta{flex-wrap:wrap;}}
.hero__cta .btn--primary,.hero__cta .btn--ghost{background:transparent;color:var(--cm-text-strong);border:1px solid var(--cm-border-strong);}
.hero__cta .btn--primary:hover,.hero__cta .btn--ghost:hover{background:var(--cm-accent);color:var(--cm-accent-contrast);border-color:var(--cm-accent);}
@media(max-width:820px){.feat{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.posts{grid-template-columns:1fr;}}
</style>
</Fragment>

<main>
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Journal</span>
  <h1 class="display-lg measure">Notes from the studio.</h1>
  <p class="lead measure">Practical guidance on physical models, project planning, materials, fabrication, and digital-to-physical production—along with news, events, and observations from Carve Model.</p>
</div></section>

<section class="section" style="padding-bottom:0;padding-top:clamp(2rem,4vw,3rem);"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Studio Updates</span>
  <article class="latest-post">
    <div>
      <span class="meta">Studio Update · Carve Studio Portal · August 11, 2026</span>
      <h3>Carve Studio Portal Is Now in Partner Testing</h3>
      <p>Carve Model is testing the Carve Studio Portal with selected partners ahead of its planned launch in January 2027. The Portal brings milestones, files, approvals, and delivery information into one shared workspace.</p>
      <a class="read" href="/blog/carve-studio-portal-partner-testing">Read the Update →</a>
    </div>
    <div class="feat-visual">
      <div class="mock" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="mock__bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>studio.physical-model.com</span></div>
        <div class="mock__body">
          <div class="mock__side">
            <div class="mock__row active"><b></b> Overview</div>
            <div class="mock__row">Milestones</div>
            <div class="mock__row">Files</div>
            <div class="mock__row">Messages</div>
            <div class="mock__row">Invoices</div>
          </div>
          <div class="mock__main">
            <div class="mock__card">
              <span class="mock__k">Active project</span>
              <div class="mock__v">Aria Tower · 1:144</div>
              <div class="mock__progress"><i style="width:68%"></i></div>
              <span class="mock__k" style="display:block;margin-top:6px;">68% · Fabrication</span>
            </div>
            <div class="mock__card">
              <span class="mock__k">Next milestone</span>
              <div class="mock__v">Finishing &amp; paint</div>
              <span class="mock__k" style="display:block;margin-top:4px;">Due in 6 days</span>
            </div>
            <div class="mock__card" style="display:flex;gap:0.6rem;align-items:center;">
              <div style="width:26px;height:26px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--cm-surface-2);flex:none;"></div>
              <div><div class="mock__v" style="font-size:0.72rem;">Studio · Maya</div><span class="mock__k">QC photos uploaded →</span></div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</div></section>

<section class="section"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Practical guides</span>
  <article class="feat">
    <div class="feat-visual">
      <span class="corner tl"></span><span class="corner br"></span>
      <img class="feat-photo" src="/assets/journal-how-to-choose.jpg" alt="Carve Model architectural scale model" style="aspect-ratio:1707/1280;">
      <span class="slot-label">Old Town Masterplan · 1:750 · ABS</span>
    </div>
    <div>
      <span class="meta">Featured guide · Scale · April 22, 2026</span>
      <h2>How to Choose the Right Scale for an Architectural Model</h2>
      <p>The right scale is determined by what the model needs to communicate, how much detail it must show, and how large the finished model can practically be.</p>
      <a class="read" href="/blog/how-to-choose-architectural-model-scale">Read the Guide →</a>
    </div>
  </article>
  <div class="posts">
    <article class="post"><span class="meta">Guide · Pricing · April 2, 2026</span><h3>How Much Does an Architectural Scale Model Cost?</h3><p>Carve Model projects start at US$4,000. Learn how scale, detail, design information, special features, schedule, and delivery requirements influence the final cost.</p><a class="read" href="/blog/architectural-scale-model-cost-us">Read →</a></article>
    <article class="post"><span class="meta">Guide · Timeline · March 18, 2026</span><h3>How Long Does It Take to Build an Architectural Scale Model?</h3><p>Most architectural models require approximately two to four weeks of production. Learn how scope, files, approvals, complexity, shipping, and installation affect the complete project timeline.</p><a class="read" href="/blog/how-long-to-build-architectural-model">Read →</a></article>
    <article class="post"><span class="meta">Guide · Model types · March 4, 2026</span><h3>Types of Architectural Models and What Each Is Used For</h3><p>From concept studies and planning models to sales-gallery, interior, site, coordination, and as-built models—learn what each type is designed to communicate and how to choose the right one.</p><a class="read" href="/blog/types-of-architectural-scale-models">Read →</a></article>
    <article class="post"><span class="meta">Guide · Digital Model Development · August 11, 2026</span><h3>From AI-Generated Image to Physical Model</h3><p>An AI-generated image can establish a compelling design direction, but it rarely contains everything required for fabrication. Learn what additional information and decisions are needed to turn a generated concept into a physical model.</p><a class="read" href="/blog/from-ai-generated-image-to-physical-model">Read →</a></article>
    <article class="post"><span class="meta">Guide · Delivery · August 11, 2026</span><h3>How Architectural Models Are Packaged, Shipped and Installed</h3><p>Successful delivery begins before fabrication. Learn how model dimensions, sectional construction, protective packaging, building access, and on-site setup are coordinated for safe transportation and installation.</p><a class="read" href="/blog/architectural-model-packaging-shipping-installation">Read →</a></article>
    <article class="post"><span class="meta">Guide · Project Planning · August 11, 2026</span><h3>How to Prepare a Brief for an Architectural Model</h3><p>A clear architectural model brief begins with purpose, audience, boundaries, dimensions, available files, and delivery requirements. Use this checklist to prepare the information needed for an initial review.</p><a class="read" href="/blog/how-to-prepare-an-architectural-model-brief">Read →</a></article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section" style="padding-top:0;"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Industry insights</span>
  <div class="posts">
    <article class="post"><span class="meta">Insight · Physical Verification · August 11, 2026</span><h3>Why Physical Verification Matters as Digital Design Becomes More Abundant</h3><p>As digital and AI-assisted tools create more design possibilities, the challenge shifts from generating options to evaluating them. Learn how physical models provide tangible evidence for clearer, more confident decisions.</p><a class="read" href="/blog/why-physical-verification-matters-in-digital-design">Read →</a></article>
    <article class="post"><span class="meta">Insight · Communication · August 11, 2026</span><h3>Physical Models, Renderings, Animation, AR and VR: What Each Communicates Best</h3><p>Physical models, renderings, animation, AR, and VR communicate different aspects of a design. Learn which medium is best for atmosphere, sequence, immersion, real-world context, and shared spatial understanding—and when they work best together.</p><a class="read" href="/blog/physical-models-vs-renderings-animation-ar-vr">Read →</a></article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section" style="padding-top:0;"><div class="container">
  <span class="eyebrow">Studio Update</span>
  <div class="posts">
    <article class="post"><span class="meta">Studio Update · AIA26 · June 16, 2026</span><h3>Carve Model at the 2026 AIA Conference in San Diego</h3><p>Carve Model attended AIA26 in San Diego. Here is what the conference reinforced about digital design, shared understanding, and the continuing role of physical models in architectural decision-making.</p><a class="read" href="/blog/carve-model-aia26-conference">Read the Update →</a></article>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="section" style="padding-top:0;"><div class="container">
  <div class="cta reveal" style="position:relative;text-align:center;background:var(--cm-black);border:1px solid var(--cm-border);border-radius:var(--r-sm);padding:clamp(3rem,6vw,5rem) var(--gutter);">
    <h2 class="display-md">Have a project in mind?</h2>
    <p class="muted mt-2" style="max-width:52ch;margin-inline:auto;">Tell us what you are creating, what information you currently have, and what the model needs to help your audience understand or decide. We will help you define an appropriate scope and scale.</p>
    <div class="hero__cta" style="justify-content:center;margin-top:2.4rem;"><a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="/contact">Get a Preliminary Estimate <span class="arrow">→</span></a></div>
  </div>
</div></section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
